// Blocky's whole move list. He is the test fighter rendered off the 3D mannequin (New Art 3D/tools/build_blocky.bat), and
// the point of him is to have a move in every slot the game knows about, each with art of its own. What every key means is
// written down at the top of fighting_moves.hor. His art plays at 12 frames a second, which is what it was rendered at, and
// every frame in here is a frame of the fight, 60 a second, so a frame of his art is 5 of them.
//
// He is the reference for how a fight is meant to feel, the Smash way. An attack on the ground plants him (walk: 0), one in the
// air keeps all of the drift, and the aerials cost a few frames if he lands in the middle of them (landing_lag).
//
//                 standing            crouching           in the air
//   X             jab                 crouching jab       jump punch (overhead)
//   Y             straight            crouching uppercut  jump punch (overhead)
//   A             high kick           low kick (low)      jump kick (overhead, knocks down)
//   B             roundhouse          sweep (low, knocks down)   jump kick
//   LeftBumper    hook, an overhead that has to be blocked standing
//   LeftTrigger   shove, next to no damage but they end up across the stage
//   RightTrigger  uppercut, the launcher. Crouching it is the crouching uppercut, which launches a little less
//   A + B         spin kick, launches and knocks down. A quarter of the meter
//   X + Y         flurry, jab, hook, straight, three hits. A quarter of the meter
//   Y + B         dragon punch, up off the ground with i-frames on the way up. Half the meter
//   A + B in the air   dive kick, straight down and forward
//   RightBumper   block, crouching block with down held
//   double tap a direction   the roll, with i-frames
//
// The uppercut (RightTrigger) puts them 90 up, above juggle height, floating down on half their gravity for 40 frames of
// hitstun, and lets him jump straight out of it the frame after it lands (hit_cancel). Jump after them, jump punch, double jump,
// jump kick. Every hit up there makes them a bit heavier (see Combat/CombatRules.cs) so it comes down by itself.
// Jab into straight links on the ground, the straight into the uppercut, and the dragon punch ends it. His normals
// cancel into the specials and the dragon punch on hit or block (hit_cancel by kind), the heavy ones cost a few frames
// when they miss (whiff_lag), and the launchers go further the more health is gone (launch_growth).

#define fight_move

let moves = {
    /* Getting around */

    idle: {
        stances: "standing",
        stance: "standing",
        phases: {
            stand: { animation: "idle", loop_while: "always", cancel: 0 }
        }
    },

    run: {
        input: "DPadLeft | DPadRight",
        trigger: "held",
        priority: 70,
        stances: "standing",
        repeat: "held",
        finish_reroutes: {
            standing: "idle"
        },
        phases: {
            stride: { animation: "run_loop", loop_while: "held", cancel: 0 },
            stop: { animation: "run_stop", until: "held", cancel: 0 }
        }
    },

    crouch: {
